 from the superior lateral portion of the nipple  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm biopsy cavity within 0 1cm of the posterior margin  This hemorrhagic biopsy cavity has a wall ranging from REMOVED_DATE to 0 8cm in thickness and is indurated with a moderate amount of fat necrosis  The cavity is slightly nodular with focally firm areas  The cavity is also within 0 4cm of the inferior margin  The remaining parenchyma is tan pink to tan white focally nodular and firm with a large amount of admixed tan yellow lobular fat  The small firm foci measure up to 0 2cm in greatest dimension within the dense tan white fibrous tissue away from the biopsy cavity  None of these firm areas appear to abut any of the inked margins  One small REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm tan pink rubbery lymph node is identified within the lateral aspect of the simple mastectomy  Representative sections are submitted as follows  H  Biopsy cavity to posterior margin I  Biopsy cavity to inferior margin J  Representative section of indurated wall biopsy cavity K  Representative section biopsy cavity to anterior superior margin L M  Representative sections away from biopsy cavity to include focally firm areas N  Lymph nodes  Gross Description by  KRISTEN SMITH Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Simon Powell  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL    EXCISION PART B  LYMPH NODES  LEFT  AXILLARY TAIL    EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Absent.
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 36 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic and blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 16 47                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 34 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast  is a 7 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast excisional biopsy specimen  with an attached 5 x 0 8cm skin ellipse  The entire specimen is inked black  with the deep margin  posterior  overinked blue  and the superior margin overinked red  It is serially sectioned from lateral to medial to reveal a tan gray  1 2cm in largest dimension  firm mass  focally abutting the anterior soft tissue margin  and 0 5cm from the posterior margin  Sectioning of the tissue away from the mass reveals a 0 6cm in largest dimension area of tan grittiness  coming to within 0 3cm of the deep margin  in the medial portion of the specimen  There is a third area of grittiness  0 2cm in largest dimension  coming to within 0 6cm of the deep margin  The remainder of the tissue is mixed white fibrous parenchyma and fatty tissue  SECTION CODE A C  Firm nodule with anterior and posterior margins  D  Representative section of nodule  E  Gritty area  F  Second gritty area  G H  Representative sections  Resident  KRISTINA M  BRAATEN  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     GROSS DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   LUMPECTOMY  AREA SUSPICIOUS FOR INVASIVE CARCINOMA CLOSE TO ANTERIOR MARGIN  O R  Resident  HOWARD CHANG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Eugene F  Ruffolo  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY   report_end  , Present.
 REMOVED_CASE_ID  SHILAS DALIA 41 F  REG REF 05 07    REMOVED_CASE_ID   WIC GRABOWSKY TARA A  M D                                                                                             Specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   REMOVED_CASE_ID  SOUT Received  05 07 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Spec Type    Clinical diagnosis   history  Baseline mammogram showed multiple clusters of indeterminate calcifications of right retroareolar lower central and upper outer quadrant    fibrocystic changes vs ductal carcinoma in situ Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ Gross description  The specimen is received in formalin in one container  labeled  stereo biopsies  right breast calcifications  and consists of two aqua cassettes  which are designated on the specimen requisition as the right retroareolar lower central breast with calcifications  The first cassette contains three firm  yellowish red needle biopsies ranging in size from 1 6cm  in length x 0 2cm  in diameter to 2 2cm  in length x 0 3cm  in diameter  3X all  labeled 1  The second aqua cassette contains a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  aggregate of reddish tan  firm  glistening needle biopsies  each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  1 agg  all  labeled 2  Also present in the same container is a 2 x 1 x 0 3cm  aggregate of reddish tan  firm needle biopsies with attached blood clot  each measuring 0 3cm  in diameter  1 agg  all  labeled 3  Dictated by  LV Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DIAGNOSIS  Right breast  lower central retroareolar  needle biopsy  Calcifications associated with atypical ductal hyperplasia  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT  NOTE  This case was reviewed by Dr  Frederick Koerner  Massachusetts General Hospital  who rendered the following opinion   I find this case especially challenging and I cannot give you a precise diagnosis  The calcifications of concern distort several ducts and ductules  and the associated ductal cells look atypical  They appear enlarged and they possess large and somewhat pleomorphic nuclei and homogeneous chromatin  A few nuclei contain conspicuous nucleoli  I would not interpret these areas as foci of ductal hyperplasia  the nuclei appear too big  and the presence of calcifications would not fit with that interpretation  The cells could represent a carcinoma  however  the foci do not exhibit an obvious increase in the number of epithelial cells  In the absence of cellular proliferation and marked anaplasia  I cannot recognize the cells as malignant  Degenerative changes can sometimes cause nuclear enlargement and pleomorphism  and such a phenomenon might explain the appearance of these cells  These degenerative effects usually cause the chromatin to become dark and smudgy rather than pale  as seen in the case at hand  so I do not feel comfortable with this interpretation  DESCRIPTIVE COMMENT   Continued  either  I would therefore make the diagnosis of atypical ductal hyperplasia and suggest that the patient undergo an excision of this region of the right breast  After examining the adjacent tissue  I expect that you will be able to reach a secure diagnosis   Final Diagnosis by  Jean L  Fraser  M D  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  MD FRAJE Notes  REMOVED_DATE  All nine slides ret d  jam  CR  REMOVED_DATE  Path report faxed  jam REMOVED_DATE  Dr  Koerner s report rec d  djd REMOVED_DATE  Sent all nine slides to Dr  Frederick Koerner   MGH via courier for opinion JLF jam  CO   617  REMOVED_DATE Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT DORD REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCODES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    Right breast  N BREANBX    BREANBX BREANBX  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     BREANBX Atypical hyperp Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJCOPIES TO  GRABOWSKY TARA A  M D  P O  Box 469 MEDFIELD  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   508 359  REMOVED_CASE_ID  SELLAND DONNA LEE M D  NEWTON WELLESLEY RADIOLOGY NEWTON  MA  REMOVED_CASE_ID   617 243  REMOVED_CASE_ID MARKERS  Breast Disease Related  Consult Case Out  Consult Case Return Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJPROCEDURES   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ  Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJ REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJTISSUES  Breast  needle biopsy   right  retroareolar  lower central Edited by  REMOVED_DATE    REMOVED_CASE_ID  PAT MURJFinal  ROSS MICHAEL J  M D    REMOVED_DATE  05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD ROSMJ FRASER JEAN L  MD      REMOVED_DATE  05 11 07  REMOVED_CASE_ID   by MD FRAJE                                                                                              , Absent.
