LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Keratin positive tumor cells are not identified on nine  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  3 Cam5 2 immunostained levels  Diagnosis by  MELINDA J  LERWILL  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 11 16                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right  block C   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Rosemary Tambouret MD Signed On  19 REMOVED_MONTH 04 at 13 48 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast 12 o clock cancer short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of tan pink fibroadipose tissue with a short black stitch designating the superior and a long black stitch the lateral margins  The posterior margin is inked black  the anterior blue  the superior green and the inferior yellow  The specimen has a localization wire in place  The specimen is serially sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal a well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm grey white  centrally hemorrhagic mass which comes to 0 1cm of the posterior  0 5cm of the superior  0 9cm of the anterior  and 1 3cm of the inferior  2 6cm of the lateral  and  3 0cm of the medial margin  A small silver metal clip is noted within the mass  Adjacent to the mass along the medial aspect is a poorly delineated REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm hemorrhagic area which abuts the inferior anterior margin and comes to 0 1cm of the medial margin  Representative sections are submitted as follows  A  Hemorrhagic area to closest margin  B E  Mass to closest margins  F  Lateral margin  radial sections   Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast biopsy posterior lesion  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm portion of tan red fibroadipose tissue with localization wire in place  No orientation is provided  The specimen is inked black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm hemorrhagic area which communicates with the margin  possibly consistent with previous biopsy site  Surrounding the defect is focally nodular dense grey white fibrous tissue  There are no discrete lesions or other gross abnormalities  The specimen is entirely submitted as G N  with the area designated by the localization wire in G J  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right axilla sentinel node  are two round tan pink rubbery lymph nodes which range from REMOVED_DATE to 2 5cm in greatest dimension  The smallest is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette O  The largest is serially sectioned and submitted entirely in cassette P Q  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin  superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm aggregate of unoriented fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette R Y  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin  inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm aggregate of unoriented cauterized fibroadipose tissue  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassette Z GG  Gross Description by  STEPHANIE KUEHN Resident  JULIA TURBINER  M D    