Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 42 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 1  SPANNING REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OF 15 LYMPH NODES  INCLUDING THE HIGHEST AXILLARY NODE   Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  02 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 11                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Right   A few tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 15 24 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name  unit number and  right breast tissue  is a right modified radical mastectomy specimen  A stitch designates the highest axillary node  The deep resection margin of the mastectomy is inked black  The mastectomy is overlaid by a REMOVED_DATE x 8 3cm ellipse of white pink skin  centered by a 4 3cm with a slightly retracted nipple  Sectioning through the breast reveals a white firm stellate area  located deep to the retracted nipple measuring 2 0cm in greatest dimension  surrounded by white yellow spiculation  This area is within at least 4 0cm of the closest  deep  resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is grossly unremarkable with extensive adipose tissue with exception of an ill defined white gray  slightly firm  nodular area  located within approximately 1 0cm of the closest  deep  resection margin  Section code  A C  Scarred area  in relation to overlying nipple D  Margin closest to scarred area E  Slightly nodular area in relation to closest margin F  Grossly unremarkable breast parenchyma in relation to resection margin G L  Lymph nodes M  Highest maxillary lymph node Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michael Ned Margolies  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Present.
