Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  03 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 44 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  LOBULAR NEOPLASIA  ATYPICAL LOBULAR HYPERPLASIA   FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES WITH MICROCALCIFICATION  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL SUPERIOR MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  RIGHT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    EXCISION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  2 CM  FOCALLY EXTENDING TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS AND FOCALLY TO THE MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic vessel invasion is not seen  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL SUPERFICIAL MARGIN    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  LEFT   FINAL SHAVED MARGIN    DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SINGLE SMALL FOCUS EXTENDING TO A CAUTERIZED SURFACE  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Invasion of the stroma  blood vessels  and lymphatic vessels is not seen  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  05 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 50                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  11 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 15 43 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  rightbreast mass with margins  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast tissue  The specimen is inked entirely in black  superiorly overlayed with green and sectioned from medial to lateral to reveal unremarkable fibrous tissue  Submitted almost entirely in cassettes A through J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number are two additional specimens  Labeled  right breast mass additional superior margin  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fatty adipose tissue which is inked and submitted entirely in cassettes K and L  Labeled  left breast  final shave margins  are multiple fragments of fibroadipose tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm in aggregate  The specimens are submitted entirely in cassettes M through R  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number and  left breast  short stitch superior  long stitch lateral  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 7 0cm fragment of breast containing 2 sutures  Inked entirely in black  superior overlayed with green  and sectioned to reveal a 2 0cm firm ill d