Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 ACCESSIONED ON  27 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 10 29 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MASTECTOMY  1  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  REMOVED_DATE CM  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED   SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE  MULTIFOCAL  PRESENT ASSOCIATED WITH AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE INVASIVE COMPONENT  AND PRESENT REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE SUPERIOR AND INFERIOR RESECTION MARGINS  3  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA TO 1 OF 13 LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Definitive blood vascular invasion is not seen  The margins of resection appear free of invasive carcinoma  SOFT TISSUE  ADDITIONAL LEFT AXILLARY TISSUE   ONE LYMPH NODE FREE OF CARCINOMA  BREAST  RIGHT   REDUCTION  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGES  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D  Signed On  01 MAY 98 at 11 23                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 MAY 98 at 16 56     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 15 03 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen consisting of a left breast with axillary tissue  30 x 23 x 9cm  a 16 x 12cm overlying skin ellipse with a ill defined  5 5cm well healed scar  and a grossly unremarkable nipple  A 3 x 2 x 2cm focally well circumscribed  round  firm solid tumor is present 8cm inferior to the nipple  0 5cm from the closest inferior inked margin  6cm from the closest deep margin  and 4cm from the closest superior inked margin  The hard  white mass is surrounded by indurated breast tissue with multiple  gritty  focally necrotic areas of breast tissue which extend approximately 3cm from the main tumor mass and extend to within 0 2cm of the superior and inferior margins   The remainder of the breast parenchyma is composed of fi